---

This project is not a fork. It was written from scratch and makes use of the
following third-party components and prior art:

  chrome-lens-py (MIT) - https://github.com/bropines/chrome-lens-py
      Installed as a pip dependency. Provides the client for Google's Lens
      Protobuf endpoint used for OCR and translation.

  jaslrobinson/circle-to-search (MIT)
      https://github.com/jaslrobinson/circle-to-search
      Prior art consulted during research. The general "freeze screen, draw a
      selection, search it" interaction concept. No source code was used.

  dinossht/lens-desktop
      https://github.com/dinossht/lens-desktop
      Prior art consulted during research. The idea of presenting search
      results in a dedicated panel rather than a full browser window. No
      source code was used.

  PyQt6 / Qt for Python (LGPLv3)
      https://pypi.org/project/PyQt6/

Google Lens is a Google service governed by Google's own terms of service.
kcircle transmits the region a user explicitly selects, in the same manner as
the official Circle to Search feature.